1
00:00:05,040 --> 00:00:11,541
When pressure builds - the pipes begin to sing.

2
00:00:16,781 --> 00:00:19,682
When the stakes rise - people start to break.

3
00:00:20,422 --> 00:00:24,062
The system is overheating…

4
00:00:24,142 --> 00:00:28,362
and someone’s turning the valve.

5
00:00:34,003 --> 00:00:38,343
America in the mirror - doesn’t recognize its face,

6
00:00:38,543 --> 00:00:41,524
The dollar trembles, inflation coils like a snake.

7
00:00:41,544 --> 00:00:44,224
Seven percent of heat - and everything smokes,

8
00:00:44,624 --> 00:00:47,764
Markets on fire, but the president stays composed.

9
00:00:47,804 --> 00:00:50,204
The Fed’s a firefighter holding gasoline,

10
00:00:50,484 --> 00:00:53,245
Under the noise of “crisis control” they calm the scene.

11
00:00:53,565 --> 00:00:56,085
Loans burn like candles on a trading chart,

12
00:00:56,525 --> 00:00:59,085
Nobody leaves - everyone plays their part.

13
00:01:00,585 --> 00:01:05,406
The system’s heating up - concrete starts to melt,

14
00:01:05,426 --> 00:01:07,686
Money turns to steam, slipping through the belt.

15
00:01:08,006 --> 00:01:10,886
Some are on the exchange, some read the news at night,

16
00:01:10,926 --> 00:01:25,467
But we’re under the same sky, buried in the same debt.

17
00:01:25,967 --> 00:01:28,568
The labor market boils, but it’s hollow inside,

18
00:01:28,788 --> 00:01:31,608
Incomes melt like ice in the heat of the ride.

19
00:01:32,048 --> 00:01:34,448
Politicians hunt for someone to blame,

20
00:01:34,468 --> 00:01:37,528
They need a storm to cover the shame of the game.

21
00:01:37,808 --> 00:01:40,369
The Fed lifts rates like a sword in the dark,

22
00:01:40,409 --> 00:01:43,549
But that sword cuts shoulders, not the heart.

23
00:01:43,909 --> 00:01:46,449
Markets will scream - they don’t really care,

24
00:01:46,709 --> 00:01:49,249
As long as the show still fills the air.

25
00:01:51,110 --> 00:01:54,290
The system’s heating up - concrete starts to melt,

26
00:01:54,310 --> 00:01:58,150
Money turns to steam, slipping through the belt.

27
00:01:58,190 --> 00:02:06,491
Some are on the exchange, some read the news at night,

28
00:02:06,811 --> 00:02:14,712
But we’re under the same sky, buried in the same debt.

29
00:02:14,772 --> 00:02:17,932
On the chart - a peak, beneath it - fear,

30
00:02:17,972 --> 00:02:20,492
Someone bought the top, someone vanished here.

31
00:02:20,552 --> 00:02:23,372
While the crowd still waits for a miracle sign,

32
00:02:23,572 --> 00:02:26,413
The elite recalculates who gets out on time.

33
00:02:26,573 --> 00:02:29,453
Every crisis feels like a brand-new spring

34
00:02:29,513 --> 00:02:32,253
For those who print wealth out of nothing.

35
00:02:32,273 --> 00:02:34,513
The common man’s just a line on a sheet,

36
00:02:34,633 --> 00:02:37,414
He believes he’ll escape - like a novel’s deceit.

37
00:02:38,654 --> 00:02:41,094
Heat isn’t weather - it’s an interest rate.

38
00:02:41,234 --> 00:02:44,414
Inflation isn’t a number - it’s a crush, a weight.

39
00:02:44,454 --> 00:02:46,874
The system overheats - but they don’t mind,

40
00:02:46,934 --> 00:02:50,595
Every crisis is a party… for the right kind.

41
00:03:05,836 --> 00:03:32,538
Everything boils, everything roars -

42
00:03:33,178 --> 00:03:39,839
but it hasn’t exploded yet.

43
00:03:40,159 --> 00:03:45,760
They call it “market stability.”

44
00:03:45,880 --> 00:03:49,420
I call it overheating.

